{
  "schema": 1,
  "goals": [
    "Describe what someone looks like and what they're like",
    "Make adjectives agree in gender and number, including irregular ones",
    "Use colours and describe hair and eyes",
    "Know when an adjective goes before the noun",
    "Form the negative with ne... pas and pas de"
  ],
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "fr-2.2-1",
      "title": "Il est grand",
      "subtitle": "Adjective agreement",
      "topics": ["adjectives", "describe"],
      "words": ["appearance#tall, big", "appearance#small", "appearance#slim", "appearance#young", "appearance#pretty", "appearance#average", "personality#nice, likeable", "personality#shy", "personality#fun, amusing", "personality#pleasant", "personality#clever, intelligent", "personality#sad", "personality#calm", "personality#funny"],
      "learn": [
        {"title": "Adjectives agree", "blocks": [
          {"type": "text", "en": "In French an adjective follows the gender and number of the noun it describes. For the feminine you add *-e*, for the plural *-s*."},
          {"type": "table", "head": ["", "masculine", "feminine"], "textCols": [0], "rows": [
            ["singular", "il est grand", "elle est grande"],
            ["plural", "ils sont grands", "elles sont grandes"]
          ]},
          {"type": "text", "en": "The final *-e* and *-s* are silent. In the feminine, though, you hear the consonant before the *-e*: *petit* [pəti] → *petite* [pətit]."},
          {"type": "tip", "title": "Ending in -e", "en": "Adjectives that already end in *-e* don't change in the feminine: *jeune, mince, timide, sympathique, calme, drôle, triste, agréable*."},
          {"type": "check", "item": {"type": "cloze", "fr": "Marie est ___.", "a": ["petite"], "hint": "small"}}
        ]},
        {"title": "Ils or elles?", "blocks": [
          {"type": "text", "en": "When you describe a group of men and women, you use the masculine plural: *Paul et Marie sont grands.*"},
          {"type": "examples", "items": [
            {"fr": "Mon frère est grand et mince.", "en": "My brother is tall and slim."},
            {"fr": "Ma sœur est petite et sympathique.", "en": "My sister is small and nice."},
            {"fr": "Mes cousines sont amusantes.", "en": "My cousins (girls) are fun."},
            {"fr": "Tom et Léa sont intelligents.", "en": "Tom and Léa are clever."}
          ]},
          {"type": "check", "item": {"type": "cloze", "fr": "Paul et Léa sont ___.", "a": ["intelligents"], "hint": "clever"}}
        ]},
        {"title": "Words", "blocks": [{"type": "vocab"}]}
      ],
      "practice": [
        {"id": "fr-2.2-1-01", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Ma mère est ___.", "a": ["mince"], "hint": "slim", "why": "Mince ends in -e, so it doesn't change in the feminine."},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-1-02", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Ma sœur est ___.", "a": ["grande"], "hint": "tall"},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-1-03", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Léa est ___.", "a": ["intelligente"], "hint": "clever"},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-1-04", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Mes cousins sont ___.", "a": ["amusants"], "hint": "fun"},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-1-05", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Mes tantes sont ___.", "a": ["agréables"], "hint": "pleasant"},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-1-06", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Julie est ___.", "a": ["timide"], "hint": "shy"},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-1-07", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Elles sont ___.", "a": ["jeunes"], "hint": "young"},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-1-08", "type": "transform", "task_en": "Make it feminine", "fr": "Il est petit.", "a": ["Elle est petite."]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-1-09", "type": "transform", "task_en": "Make it feminine", "fr": "Il est intelligent.", "a": ["Elle est intelligente."]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-1-10", "type": "transform", "task_en": "Make it feminine", "fr": "Il est timide.", "a": ["Elle est timide."]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-1-11", "type": "transform", "task_en": "Make it plural", "fr": "Elle est grande.", "a": ["Elles sont grandes."]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-1-12", "type": "build", "en": "My sister is small and slim.", "a": ["Ma sœur est petite et mince."]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-1-13", "type": "build", "en": "My brother is tall and funny.", "a": ["Mon frère est grand et drôle."]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-1-14", "type": "build", "en": "Paul and Marie are young.", "a": ["Paul et Marie sont jeunes."]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-1-15", "type": "order", "en": "My friend (a girl) is clever and fun.", "a": ["Mon amie est intelligente et amusante", "Ma copine est intelligente et amusante"], "extra": ["intelligent", "ma"]}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "fr-2.2-2",
      "title": "Elle est sportive",
      "subtitle": "Special adjective forms",
      "topics": ["adjectives", "describe"],
      "words": ["personality#lazy", "personality#sporty", "personality#active", "personality#generous", "personality#boring", "personality#chatty, talkative", "personality#hard-working", "personality#stingy", "personality#sincere", "personality#nervous", "personality#kind", "personality#nasty, mean", "personality#serious", "personality#curious", "personality#happy", "appearance#fat", "appearance#old", "appearance#beautiful", "appearance#new"],
      "learn": [
        {"title": "Special endings", "blocks": [
          {"type": "table", "head": ["ending", "masculine", "feminine"], "rows": [
            ["-eux → -euse", "paresseux, sérieux", "paresseuse, sérieuse"],
            ["-if → -ive", "sportif, actif", "sportive, active"],
            ["-eur → -euse", "travailleur, menteur", "travailleuse, menteuse"],
            ["-en → -enne", "italien", "italienne"],
            ["-er → -ère", "cher", "chère"]
          ]},
          {"type": "text", "en": "*Heureux, curieux, ennuyeux, généreux, nerveux* behave like *sérieux*: *heureuse, curieuse, ennuyeuse, généreuse, nerveuse*."},
          {"type": "tip", "title": "avare, sincère", "en": "*Avare* (stingy) and *sincère* (sincere) end in *-e*, so they don't change in the feminine."},
          {"type": "check", "item": {"type": "cloze", "fr": "Ma sœur est très ___.", "a": ["sportive"], "hint": "sporty"}}
        ]},
        {"title": "Irregular adjectives", "blocks": [
          {"type": "table", "head": ["", "masculine", "feminine"], "textCols": [0], "rows": [
            ["beautiful", "beau", "belle"],
            ["new", "nouveau", "nouvelle"],
            ["old", "vieux", "vieille"],
            ["kind", "gentil", "gentille"],
            ["fat", "gros", "grosse"],
            ["white", "blanc", "blanche"],
            ["long", "long", "longue"],
            ["frank", "franc", "franche"]
          ]},
          {"type": "text", "en": "In the plural, words ending in *-s* or *-x* don't change: *Ils sont sérieux.* *Beau* and *nouveau* take *-x*: *beaux, nouveaux*."},
          {"type": "check", "item": {"type": "cloze", "fr": "Ma grand-mère est très ___.", "a": ["gentille"], "hint": "kind"}}
        ]},
        {"title": "Words", "blocks": [{"type": "vocab"}]}
      ],
      "practice": [
        {"id": "fr-2.2-2-01", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Elle est ___.", "a": ["paresseuse"], "hint": "lazy"},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-2-02", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Ma tante est ___.", "a": ["travailleuse"], "hint": "hard-working"},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-2-03", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Léa est ___.", "a": ["active"], "hint": "active"},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-2-04", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Mes cousines sont ___.", "a": ["curieuses"], "hint": "curious"},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-2-05", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Ma mère est ___.", "a": ["heureuse"], "hint": "happy"},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-2-06", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Julie est ___.", "a": ["belle"], "hint": "beautiful"},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-2-07", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Ma grand-mère est ___.", "a": ["vieille"], "hint": "old"},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-2-08", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Mes frères sont ___.", "a": ["beaux"], "hint": "handsome"},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-2-09", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Elles sont ___.", "a": ["bavardes"], "hint": "chatty"},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-2-10", "type": "transform", "task_en": "Make it feminine", "fr": "Il est sérieux.", "a": ["Elle est sérieuse."]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-2-11", "type": "transform", "task_en": "Make it feminine", "fr": "Il est gentil.", "a": ["Elle est gentille."]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-2-12", "type": "transform", "task_en": "Make it feminine", "fr": "Il est généreux.", "a": ["Elle est généreuse."]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-2-13", "type": "transform", "task_en": "Make it feminine", "fr": "Il est nouveau.", "a": ["Elle est nouvelle."]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-2-14", "type": "transform", "task_en": "Make it plural", "fr": "Il est ennuyeux.", "a": ["Ils sont ennuyeux."], "why": "Words ending in -x don't change in the plural."},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-2-15", "type": "build", "en": "My sister is sporty and active.", "a": ["Ma sœur est sportive et active."]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-2-16", "type": "build", "en": "My grandfather is old but kind.", "a": ["Mon grand-père est vieux, mais gentil."]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-2-17", "type": "build", "en": "She is lazy and boring.", "a": ["Elle est paresseuse et ennuyeuse."]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-2-18", "type": "order", "en": "My aunt is very generous.", "a": ["Ma tante est très généreuse"], "extra": ["généreux", "mon"]}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "fr-2.2-3",
      "title": "Les couleurs",
      "subtitle": "Colours and agreement",
      "topics": ["adjectives"],
      "words": ["colors#colour", "colors#blue", "colors#green", "colors#black", "colors#grey", "colors#white", "colors#purple", "colors#red", "colors#yellow", "colors#pink", "colors#brown", "colors#orange", "colors#beige", "colors#light (colour)", "colors#dark (colour)"],
      "learn": [
        {"title": "Colours", "blocks": [
          {"type": "table", "head": ["", "masculine", "feminine"], "textCols": [0], "rows": [
            ["blue", "bleu", "bleue"], ["green", "vert", "verte"], ["black", "noir", "noire"], ["grey", "gris", "grise"],
            ["white", "blanc", "blanche"], ["purple", "violet", "violette"], ["red", "rouge", "rouge"], ["yellow", "jaune", "jaune"],
            ["pink", "rose", "rose"], ["brown", "marron", "marron"], ["orange", "orange", "orange"]
          ]},
          {"type": "text", "en": "A colour goes **after** the noun and agrees with it: *un chat noir, une voiture verte, des fleurs jaunes*."},
          {"type": "tip", "title": "marron and orange", "en": "*Marron* and *orange* never change, not even in the plural: *des yeux marron, des chaussures orange*. They were originally the names of fruits (chestnut, orange)."},
          {"type": "check", "item": {"type": "cloze", "fr": "Une voiture ___.", "a": ["verte"], "hint": "green"}}
        ]},
        {"title": "Light and dark", "blocks": [
          {"type": "text", "en": "*Clair* (light) and *foncé* (dark) go after the colour, and then the whole phrase doesn't change: *une robe bleu clair, des yeux vert foncé*."},
          {"type": "examples", "items": [
            {"fr": "Mon chat est noir et blanc.", "en": "My cat is black and white."},
            {"fr": "Ma chambre est bleu clair.", "en": "My bedroom is light blue."},
            {"fr": "J'adore la couleur orange.", "en": "I love the colour orange."}
          ]}
        ]},
        {"title": "Words", "blocks": [{"type": "vocab"}]}
      ],
      "practice": [
        {"id": "fr-2.2-3-01", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Un chat ___.", "a": ["noir"], "hint": "black"},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-3-02", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Une maison ___.", "a": ["blanche"], "hint": "white"},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-3-03", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Des chiens ___.", "a": ["gris"], "hint": "grey", "why": "Gris ends in -s, so it doesn't change in the plural."},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-3-04", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Des fleurs ___.", "a": ["jaunes"], "hint": "yellow"},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-3-05", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Une fleur ___.", "a": ["violette"], "hint": "purple"},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-3-06", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Des yeux ___.", "a": ["marron"], "hint": "brown", "why": "Marron doesn't change, not even in the plural."},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-3-07", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Une voiture ___.", "a": ["bleue"], "hint": "blue"},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-3-08", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Des voitures ___.", "a": ["orange"], "hint": "orange"},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-3-09", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Une robe ___.", "a": ["rouge"], "hint": "red"},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-3-10", "type": "build", "en": "I have a black cat.", "a": ["J'ai {un chat noir|une chatte noire}."]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-3-11", "type": "build", "en": "The house is white and the garden is green.", "a": ["La maison est blanche et le jardin est vert."]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-3-12", "type": "build", "en": "My car is grey.", "a": ["Ma voiture est grise."]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-3-13", "type": "order", "en": "I like pink and purple flowers.", "a": ["J'aime les fleurs roses et violettes"], "extra": ["rose", "violet"]}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "fr-2.2-4",
      "title": "Les yeux bleus",
      "subtitle": "Hair, eyes and word order",
      "topics": ["adjectives", "describe"],
      "words": ["body#hair", "body#eyes", "body#eye", "body#face", "appearance#blond (hair)", "appearance#dark brown (hair)", "appearance#red (hair)", "appearance#chestnut brown (hair)", "appearance#short", "appearance#long", "appearance#straight (hair)", "appearance#wavy", "appearance#curly"],
      "learn": [
        {"title": "Hair and eyes", "blocks": [
          {"type": "text", "en": "You describe appearance with *avoir* and the definite article: *J'ai les cheveux blonds.* (I have blond hair.) *Il a les yeux bleus.* (He has blue eyes.) *Cheveux* and *yeux* are masculine plural, so *blonds, bleus*."},
          {"type": "table", "textCols": [0], "rows": [
            ["blond hair", "les cheveux blonds"],
            ["tmavé vlasy", "les cheveux bruns"],
            ["zrzavé vlasy", "les cheveux roux"],
            ["chestnut brown hair", "les cheveux châtains"],
            ["short / long hair", "les cheveux courts / longs"],
            ["rovné / vlnité / kudrnaté", "raides / ondulés / frisés"],
            ["blue / green / brown eyes", "les yeux bleus / verts / marron"]
          ]},
          {"type": "tip", "title": "un œil, des yeux", "en": "One eye is *un œil*, eyes are *des yeux*. A completely different word!"},
          {"type": "check", "item": {"type": "build", "en": "I have brown eyes.", "a": ["J'ai les yeux marron."]}}
        ]},
        {"title": "Before or after?", "blocks": [
          {"type": "text", "en": "Most adjectives go **after** the noun: *un garçon timide, une fille sportive*. A few short, common ones go **before** it: *grand, petit, jeune, vieux, beau, joli, nouveau, bon, mauvais*. For example *une petite sœur, un grand frère, une jolie maison*."},
          {"type": "tip", "title": "bel, nouvel, vieil", "en": "Before a vowel, *beau, nouveau, vieux* have a special form: *un bel homme, un nouvel ami, un vieil oncle*."},
          {"type": "examples", "items": [
            {"fr": "J'ai un grand frère et une petite sœur.", "en": "I have an older brother and a younger sister."},
            {"fr": "C'est une fille très sympathique.", "en": "She's a very nice girl."},
            {"fr": "Mon père a les cheveux courts et les yeux verts.", "en": "My dad has short hair and green eyes."}
          ]},
          {"type": "check", "item": {"type": "cloze", "fr": "J'ai une ___ sœur.", "a": ["petite"], "hint": "small"}}
        ]},
        {"title": "Words", "blocks": [{"type": "vocab"}]}
      ],
      "practice": [
        {"id": "fr-2.2-4-01", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Elle a les cheveux ___.", "a": ["blonds"], "hint": "blond"},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-4-02", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Il a les yeux ___.", "a": ["verts"], "hint": "green"},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-4-03", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Mon père a les cheveux ___.", "a": ["courts"], "hint": "short"},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-4-04", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Ma sœur a les cheveux ___.", "a": ["longs"], "hint": "long"},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-4-05", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Léa a les cheveux ___.", "a": ["roux"], "hint": "red (hair)"},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-4-06", "type": "cloze", "fr": "J'ai un ___ ami.", "a": ["nouvel"], "hint": "new", "why": "Before a vowel, nouveau becomes nouvel."},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-4-07", "type": "build", "en": "I have blond hair and blue eyes.", "a": ["J'ai les cheveux blonds et les yeux bleus."]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-4-08", "type": "build", "en": "He (or she) has short dark hair.", "a": ["{Il|Elle} a les cheveux {courts et bruns|bruns et courts}."]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-4-09", "type": "build", "en": "I have a younger sister and an older brother.", "a": ["J'ai une petite sœur et un grand frère."]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-4-10", "type": "build", "en": "He's a nice boy.", "a": ["C'est un garçon sympathique."]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-4-11", "type": "build", "en": "My grandmother has curly hair.", "a": ["Ma grand-mère a les cheveux frisés."]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-4-12", "type": "transform", "task_en": "Describe a girl (feminine)", "fr": "C'est un petit garçon blond.", "a": ["C'est une petite fille blonde."]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-4-13", "type": "order", "en": "My friend (a boy) has brown eyes.", "a": ["Mon copain a les yeux marron", "Mon ami a les yeux marron"], "extra": ["marrons", "est"]}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "fr-2.2-5",
      "title": "Je ne suis pas timide",
      "subtitle": "The negative ne... pas",
      "topics": ["negation"],
      "words": ["basics#no", "basics#not at all", "appearance#ugly", "personality#unlikeable", "personality#optimistic", "personality#pessimistic", "personality#pleased, content", "personality#crazy, mad"],
      "learn": [
        {"title": "The negative ne... pas", "blocks": [
          {"type": "text", "en": "A French negative has two parts that go around the verb: *ne* + verb + *pas*. *Je suis timide. → Je ne suis pas timide.* Before a vowel *ne* shortens to *n'*: *Il n'est pas grand.*"},
          {"type": "examples", "items": [
            {"fr": "Je ne suis pas français.", "en": "I'm not French. (boy)"},
            {"fr": "Elle n'est pas sportive.", "en": "She isn't sporty."},
            {"fr": "Nous ne sommes pas frères.", "en": "We aren't brothers."},
            {"fr": "Il n'est pas du tout timide.", "en": "He isn't shy at all."}
          ]},
          {"type": "tip", "title": "Reflexive verbs", "en": "With reflexive verbs *ne* goes before the pronoun: *Je ne m'appelle pas Paul.*"},
          {"type": "check", "item": {"type": "transform", "task_en": "Make it negative", "fr": "Je suis grand.", "a": ["Je ne suis pas grand."]}}
        ]},
        {"title": "pas de", "blocks": [
          {"type": "text", "en": "After a negative, *un, une, des* become *de* (*d'* before a vowel): *J'ai un frère. → Je n'ai pas de frère.* *J'ai un animal. → Je n'ai pas d'animal.*"},
          {"type": "text", "en": "The definite article *le, la, les* doesn't change after a negative: *Il n'a pas les yeux bleus.* And after *être* nothing changes: *Ce n'est pas un chat.*"},
          {"type": "tip", "title": "In speech", "en": "In everyday speech *ne* is often dropped: *Je suis pas timide.* At school and in tests, always write it."},
          {"type": "check", "item": {"type": "transform", "task_en": "Make it negative", "fr": "J'ai une sœur.", "a": ["Je n'ai pas de sœur."]}}
        ]},
        {"title": "Words", "blocks": [{"type": "vocab"}]}
      ],
      "practice": [
        {"id": "fr-2.2-5-01", "type": "transform", "task_en": "Make it negative", "fr": "Il est timide.", "a": ["Il n'est pas timide."]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-5-02", "type": "transform", "task_en": "Make it negative", "fr": "Nous sommes tchèques.", "a": ["{Nous ne sommes pas|On n'est pas} tchèques."]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-5-03", "type": "transform", "task_en": "Make it negative", "fr": "J'ai un chien.", "a": ["Je n'ai pas de chien."]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-5-04", "type": "transform", "task_en": "Make it negative", "fr": "Elle a des frères.", "a": ["Elle n'a pas de frères."]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-5-05", "type": "transform", "task_en": "Make it negative", "fr": "J'ai un animal.", "a": ["Je n'ai pas d'animal."]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-5-06", "type": "transform", "task_en": "Make it negative", "fr": "Il a les yeux verts.", "a": ["Il n'a pas les yeux verts."], "why": "The definite article les doesn't change after a negative."},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-5-07", "type": "transform", "task_en": "Make it negative", "fr": "Je m'appelle Marc.", "a": ["Je ne m'appelle pas Marc."]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-5-08", "type": "transform", "task_en": "Make it negative", "fr": "C'est un chat.", "a": ["Ce n'est pas un chat."], "why": "After être, un doesn't change to de."},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-5-09", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Je ___ suis pas grand.", "a": ["ne"]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-5-10", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Il ___ pas français.", "a": ["n'est"], "hint": "negative + être"},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-5-11", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Je n'ai pas ___ frère.", "a": ["de"]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-5-12", "type": "cloze", "fr": "Tu n'as pas ___animal ?", "a": ["d'"]},
        {"id": "fr-2.2-5-13", "type": "build", "en": "I'm not shy.", "a": ["Je ne suis pas timide."]},
